comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T17:09:33.832Z","harness:claude-code","Re-measured live on 2026-07-26 after the v2026.7.26 release that shipped pm-03pq3o. The census now covers 37,202 history entries across the whole workspace, including roughly 3,500 entries this session wrote through the current build with the current harness: agent_model is present on 0 of 37,202, and no entry carries a session field either. Harness detection itself is healthy in the same census — claude-code 2,363, codex 570, opencode 66 — which isolates the failure precisely to the model dimension rather than to detection as a whole. No key matching effort or thinking appears anywhere in the entry schema, which is the pm-itsjf0 half. So the plumbing that pm-03pq3o and pm-brxdct shipped remains correct and inert: the descriptor still names ANTHROPIC_MODEL and CLAUDE_MODEL for claude-code and this harness sets neither, so a fresh release did not move the number."
  "2026-07-27T06:22:57.917Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence 2026-07-27: tracker-linked tests pass for every item; CI=1 pnpm lint passes ESLint, zero jscpd clones, static quality, 100% docstrings, package boundary, token budget, SDK surface/import-cost/transport ratchets; 377 files and 6,448 tests pass at exact 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Fresh packed acceptance passed npx, Bun SDK import, bunx, an unrelated npm prefix with resolved executable containment, 86-action SDK/CLI completeness with zero unclassified inputs, three provenance dimensions, durable CLI model/effort/role history, and the 88-command package-first dogfood flow. TOON 4.1 passed a 2,127-item storage integrity read, the earlier 2,125-item read/serialize/read corpus sweep, 250-run adversarial properties, and fail-closed negative controls. Secret scan, pnpm audit, GitHub Dependabot/code/secret scanning, open PR inventory, and open-issue PM-link inventory are all clean; only canonically deferred incompatible Sentry, npm-package-arg, and TypeScript upgrades remain. Live pm validate reports zero history drift, zero storage failures, and only the existing 290 historical resolution warnings; pm health is healthy with real-time telemetry draining."
  "2026-07-27T06:26:36.654Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: broad SDK parity, agent provenance, and TOON durability delivery published as GitHub PR #765 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/765 at implementation head 46e26717fa913cc2caa4914c730e77e75bae693a. Exact-head checks and AI review loop are pending."
  "2026-07-31T14:15:16.968Z","harness:claude-code","Closed-item conformance check 2026-07-31. Recorded here so the closed record does not continue to read as if practical model capture were achieved; no reopen is proposed, because the shipped channels and the shipped analysis both match this item's resolution text.\n\nThis item's title states the condition as zero of 35,103 recorded entries carrying a model. Measured today over 44,408 entries: 2,814 carry a model key and all 2,814 are explicit nulls, so observed model count corpus-wide is still zero, including every entry written in the four days since this closed. The actual_result recorded here - 'Installed CLI history persisted gpt-5.6-sol with override source' - is reproducible and is the override channel, which requires PM_AGENT_MODEL to be set by hand. The automatic detection channels have not produced an observation on any real entry.\n\nThe live gap is tracked by the open pm-ffz0a9, which now carries this measurement plus a same-session probe showing effort resolving from CLAUDE_EFFORT while model resolves to an explicit null in the same entry. Two adjacent mechanism defects found the same day: pm-9wbiye (explicit-unavailable is written for the model dimension only) and pm-1wiugq (the coverage analyzer this item delivered has no consumer outside its own unit test, so the inert condition it detects has never been reported)."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T03:00:04.515Z","harness:claude-code","Re-measured 2026-07-28 across the full corpus, 40,353 entries. Two things changed since this item was written and one scoping conclusion is now firm.\n\nWhat SHIPPED: entries now carry an agent_provenance object, present on 807 entries, and it holds the model slot plus an effort sub-object. Effort capture WORKS - my own entries this session read agent_provenance.effort = {value: \"xhigh\", source: \"environment\"}, resolved from CLAUDE_EFFORT. agent_instance is also live on 5,108 entries. So the plumbing this item needed is complete: there is a field, it is populated for a sibling dimension, and the entry shape is right.\n\nWhat has NOT changed: agent_model and agent_provenance.model are null on 40,353 of 40,353 entries. Not one recorded entry in the history of this workspace carries a model. Harness detection meanwhile is healthy - agent_harness is populated on 6,143 entries across three distinct harnesses, claude-code 4,350, codex 1,638, opencode 155.\n\nThe scoping conclusion, which changes what the fix is: the model is NOT obtainable from the environment on this harness. A live dump of the claude-code process environment shows exactly these keys - CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_BRIDGE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT, CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_EFFORT, CLAUDE_PID. There is no ANTHROPIC_MODEL, no CLAUDE_MODEL, and no other key naming a model. Adding more spellings to model_environment_keys therefore cannot fix this, because the value being looked for is not published to the environment at all.\n\nSo the remaining work is to choose a different SOURCE, not a different key. The options worth weighing at fix time: derive it from the harness's own version or session metadata reachable via CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH, accept an explicit configured value, or let the SDK caller supply it and record the source honestly as asserted rather than detected. Whichever is chosen, effort already demonstrates the right pattern - it records both a value and a source, so a supplied model can be distinguished from a detected one without weakening the provenance guarantee.\n\nNote the effort precedent also settles the companion question on the descriptor-extensibility item: a dimension outside the original three-key schema was added and is populating correctly, so the schema is no longer the blocker."
